  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The relevant information is the pairwise differences in outcomes between Lottery A and Lottery B. The outcomes are: A has -3000€ (0.2%) and 0€ (99.8%); B has -6000€ (0.1%) and 0€ (99.9%). The pairwise outcome differences are computed as follows: (-3000) - (-6000) = +3000 (when A yields -3000 and B yields -6000), (-3000) - 0 = -3000 (when A yields -3000 and B yields 0), 0 - (-6000) = +6000 (when A yields 0 and B yields -6000), and 0 - 0 = 0 (when both yield 0). The sum of all pairwise outcome differences is +3000 - 3000 + 6000 + 0 = +6000. Since the sum is positive, this favors Lottery A (the one with the smaller loss in the adverse event). Thus, the reason would prefer Lottery A based on a more favorable sum of outcome differences.",
