{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The relevant information involves computing the pairwise differences between outcomes of Lottery A and Lottery B. Lottery A has two outcomes: +3000 (50%) and -3000 (50%). Lottery B has one outcome: +1000 (100%). To compute pairwise differences, we compare each outcome of A with each outcome of B. There are two pairs: (3000, 1000) and (-3000, 1000). The differences are: 3000 - 1000 = +2000, and -3000 - 1000 = -4000. The sum of outcome differences is +2000 + (-4000) = -2000. Since this sum is negative, the difference favors Lottery B. Thus, the rule of the decision reason would prefer Lottery B due to the more favorable (less unfavorable) sum of pairwise outcome differences.",
